prompt.raw:
I have a Go function that fetches a list of URLs concurrently and
returns the response bodies. It mostly works but sometimes returns
wrong results — some slots in the results slice end up with the
wrong body or are empty even when the request succeeded. I'm also
seeing what looks like a file descriptor leak under load. Go 1.21.
What's wrong with this code?

```go
func fetchAll(urls []string) []string {
    results := make([]string, len(urls))
    var wg sync.WaitGroup
    for i, url := range urls {
        wg.Add(1)
        go func() {
            defer wg.Done()
            resp, err := http.Get(url)
            if err != nil {
              return
            }
            body, _ := io.ReadAll(resp.Body)
            results[i] = string(body)
        }()
    }
    wg.Wait()
    return results
}
```

